    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nindent\n\n### Description\n\nWhen the indent marker is displayed and you use:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.opt.listchars       = { tab     = '»·', }\r\n```\r\n\r\nThen the it will remove the listchar for indented code for more than one level.\r\n\r\n![ident_with_tab_listchar](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/545480/189061539-c9f2081f-38f0-4763-93da-d16013eebec1.png)\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.7.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. In your config set:\r\n```lua\r\nvim.opt.listchars       = { tab     = '»·', }\r\n```\r\n2. configure mini.nvim indent\r\n3. Open source code with tabs e.g. Samba source code\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe listchar should not be removed by the indent marker.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe listchar is removed by the indent marker. See image above.",
